load 0
=== sambamba
--- sambamba 
depth 	output statistics (BAM)
flagstat 	output statistics (BAM)
index 	build index (BAI)
markdup 	mark or remove duplicates (BAM)
merge 	merge files (BAM)
mpileup 	parallel execution of samtools (BAM)
slice 	slice file (BAM using BED)
sort 	sort file (BAM)
subsample 	subsample (BAM)
validate 	simple validator (BAM)
view 	view contents and convert from one format to another (SAM/BAM/JSON/UNPACK)
--- sambamba m
markdup 	mark or remove duplicates (BAM)
merge 	merge files (BAM)
mpileup 	parallel execution of samtools (BAM)
--- sambamba view -
--num-filter=	filter flag bits: 'i1/i2' is samtools' -f i1 -F i2
--subsampling-seed=	set seed for subsampling
-F 	keep only the reads that satisfy FILTER
-H 	print only the header
-I 	output to stdout only reference names and lengths in JSON
-L 	output only reads overlapping one of regions from the BED file
-S 	the input is SAM
-T 	the reference, for writing CRAM
-c 	print only the number of matching records
-f 	the output format
-h 	print the header before the reads
-l 	the compression level (0 to 9)
-o 	the output file
-p 	show a progress bar on standard error
-s 	subsample reads (read pairs)
-t 	maximum number of threads to use
-v 	output only valid alignments
--- sambamba view --for
--format=	the output format
--- sambamba view -f 
bam 
json 
sam 
unpack 
--- sambamba view -L data/
data/peaks.bed 
data/sub/
--- sambamba view data/
data/a.bam 
data/b.sam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- sambamba view data/a.bam 
chrA 
chrB 
--- sambamba index data/
data/a.bam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- sambamba index -F data/
data/genome.fa 
data/sub/
--- sambamba sort --tmpdir data/
data/sub/
--- sambamba markdup data/
data/a.bam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- sambamba subsample --logging 
critical 
debug 
info 
warning 
--- sambamba depth 
base 	the depth of each base
region 	the depth of each region of a BED file
window 	the depth of windows along the genome
--- sambamba depth window --
--annotate 	mark records that fail the criteria with a column of y/n instead of skipping them
--combined 	output combined statistics for all samples
--cov-threshold=	a coverage threshold: a column with the percentage of bases above it
--filter=	a custom filter for alignments
--fix-mate-overlaps 	detect overlaps of mate reads and handle them on per-base basis
--max-coverage=	maximum mean coverage for output
--min-base-quality=	don't count bases with lower base quality
--min-coverage=	minimum mean coverage for output
--nthreads=	maximum number of threads to use
--output-file=	output filename
--overlap=	overlap of successive windows, in bp
--window-size=	breadth of the window, in bp (required)
--- sambamba depth region -T 
--- sambamba depth region -L data/
data/peaks.bed 
data/sub/
--- sambamba mpileup --s
--samtools 	the arguments of samtools mpileup follow
=== bamtools
--- bamtools 
convert 	converts between BAM and a number of other formats
count 	prints number of alignments in BAM file(s)
coverage 	prints coverage statistics from the input BAM file
filter 	filters BAM file(s) by user-specified criteria
header 	prints BAM header information
help 	show the help of a command
index 	generates index for BAM file
merge 	merge multiple BAM files into single file
random 	select random alignments from BAM file(s)
resolve 	resolves paired-end reads (marking the IsProperPair flag as needed)
revert 	removes duplicate marks and restores original base qualities
sort 	sorts the BAM file according to some criteria
split 	split a BAM file on a property, a BAM file for each value
stats 	prints some basic statistics from input BAM file(s)
--- bamtools filter -isP
-isPaired 	keep only alignments that were sequenced as paired?
-isPrimaryAlignment 	keep only alignments marked as primary?
-isProperPair 	keep only alignments that passed PE resolution?
--- bamtools filter -isPaired 
false 
true 
--- bamtools convert -format 
bed 
fasta 
fastq 
json 
pileup 
sam 
yaml 
--- bamtools convert -in data/
data/a.bam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- bamtools convert -fasta data/
data/genome.fa 
data/sub/
--- bamtools help 
convert 
count 
coverage 
filter 
header 
index 
merge 
random 
resolve 
revert 
sort 
split 
stats 
=== samblaster, mosdepth, cramino
--- samblaster --max
--maxReadLength=	maximum length of SEQ/QUAL in the input
--maxSplitCount=	maximum number of split alignments of a read in the splitter file
--maxUnmappedBases=	maximum number of unaligned bases between two alignments in the splitter file
--- samblaster -i data/
data/a.bam 
data/b.sam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- mosdepth -
--d4 	output per-base depth in d4 format
-F 	exclude reads with any of the bits in FLAG set
-Q 	mapping quality threshold
-R 	only calculate depth for these comma-separated read groups IDs
-T 	for each interval in --by, write number of bases covered by at least threshold bases
-a 	count the coverage of the full fragment including the full insert (proper pairs only)
-b 	optional BED file or (integer) window-sizes
-c 	chromosome to restrict depth calculation
-f 	fasta file for use with CRAM files
-h 	show help
-i 	only include reads with any of the bits in FLAG set
-l 	minimum insert size
-m 	output median of each region (in --by) instead of mean
-n 	dont output per-base depth
-q 	write quantized output see docs for description
-t 	number of BAM decompression threads
-u 	maximum insert size
-x 	dont look at internal cigar operations or correct mate overlaps
--- mosdepth -b data/
data/peaks.bed 
data/sub/
--- mosdepth out data/
data/a.bam 
data/c.cram 
data/sub/
--- mosdepth -c 
--- cramino --format 
json 
text 
tsv 
--- cramino --hi
--hist	if histograms have to be generated (optionally specify output file as --hist=FILE)
--hist-count	output read length histogram bin counts in TSV format
--- cramino --reference data/
data/genome.fa 
data/sub/
=== vcftools
--- vcftools --gz
--gzdiff=	a gzipped VCF file to compare with
--gzvcf=	a gzipped VCF file to process
--- vcftools --gzvcf data/
data/calls.vcf.gz 
data/sub/
--- vcftools --bed data/
data/peaks.bed 
data/sub/
--- vcftools --gzvcf data/calls.vcf.gz --chr 
chr1 
chr2 
--- vcftools --gzvcf data/calls.vcf.gz --indv 
sampleA 
sampleB 
--- vcftools --TsTv
--TsTv-by-count 	Ts/Tv ratio by alternative allele count
--TsTv-by-qual 	Ts/Tv ratio by quality
--TsTv-summary 	summary of transitions and transversions
--TsTv=	Ts/Tv ratio in bins of this size
